<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">

   <teiHeader>
 
      <fileDesc>
         <titleStmt>
            <title>Mary Behrend's Letters</title>
            <author>Mary Behrend</author>
            <respStmt>
               <resp>Encoded by</resp>
               <name>Kaa Rivera</name>
            </respStmt>
         </titleStmt>
         <publicationStmt>
            <publisher>Friendship Calendar Co.</publisher>
            <date>1908</date>
            <availability>
               <p>Freely available at the Penn State Behrend Library</p>
            </availability>
         </publicationStmt>
         <sourceDesc>
            <p>Physical calendar pages</p>
            <p>A collection of handwritten letters and drawings from Mary "Molly" Behrend to her
               husband, Ernest Behrend.</p>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
   </teiHeader>
   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="calendar" n="1">
            <dateline><emph rend="#blue-color">M</emph>arch 11, 1909</dateline>
            <p>Thursday</p>
            <figure place="center">
               <!--Attempting to insert a graphic here: -->
               <graphic url="cal-1"/>
               <figDesc>Four drawings of elegantly dressed women in brightly colored dresses point
                  at each other, presumably in the midst of a teaparty.</figDesc>
            </figure>
            <fw type="hand" place="bottom-center">Everybody dressed in their best, for <emph
                  rend="underline">this</emph> is an <emph rend="underline">Erie</emph>
               <emph rend="underline">Tea</emph>. They <emph rend="underline">eat</emph> too much, <emph rend="b"
                  >talk</emph> too much. You can bet they drink <unclear reason="illegible">rope
                  in</unclear> me</fw>
            <!--Unsure of how to add the xml ids...-->
            <fw rend="red-ink"/>
         </div>
         <div type="calendar" n="2">
            <dateline><emph rend="#red-color">M</emph>arch 12, 1909</dateline>
            <p>Friday</p>
            <figure place="center">
               <graphic url="cal-2"/>
               <figDesc>A drawing of Molly "Mary" wearing large snow shoes.</figDesc>
            </figure>
            <fw type="hand" place="right-center">Molly on snowshoes that Mr. Weir got. Pretty
               picture is it not?!</fw>
            <fw rend="#red-ink" place="bottom-right" type="hand"><unclear reason="illegible">Love
                  you Molly.</unclear></fw>
         </div>
         <div type="calendar" n="3">
            <dateline><emph rend="#red-color">F</emph>ebruary 16,1909 </dateline>
            <p>Tuesday</p>
            <figure>
               <graphic url="cal-3"/>
               <figDesc>A drawing of Mr. Behrend holding what appears to be a bed bug, standing in
                  front of a canpoy bed. </figDesc>
            </figure>
            <fw type="hand" place="bottom-center">Mr. <unclear reason="illegible">Behrend</unclear>
               finds a bed bug!</fw>
            <fw type="hand" place="bottom-center" rend="#red-ink">I wonder if you have found many
               lately! </fw>
         </div>
         <div type="calendar" n="4">
            <dateline><emph rend="#green-color">M</emph>arch 17, 1909</dateline>
            <p>Wednesday</p>
            <p>St. Patrick's Day</p>
            <figure>
               <graphic url="cal-4"/>
               <figDesc>Small green four leaf clover drawings are scattered across the page, along
                  with two small snakes. One snake sits curled just below the dateline, while the
                  other is stretched out to the right of the date.</figDesc>
            </figure>
            <fw type="hand" place="center">St. Patrick was a <unclear reason = "illegible">useful</unclear> saint. He frightened all the
               snakes away -- I wish he'd try his art on <emph rend = "underline">smoke</emph> around the Hammermill some day!</fw>
            <figure place="bottom-right">
               <figDesc>A drawing of the Hammermill factory sits in the bottom-right corner of the
                  calendar page, with black smoke coming out of the exhausts.</figDesc>
            </figure>
            <!-- I could not figure out the last two words of this line -->
            <fw rend="#red-ink" place="bottom" type="hand">The Hammermill really <unclear reason="illegible"></unclear></fw>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
</TEI>
